# CQ 05: Which controls state no controlled variable?
#
# Entry 351-42-09 defines the controlled variable as the variable of the
# controlled system that the control acts on. A control without one acts on
# nothing a model can name, so nothing can be said about what it achieves.
#
# Legitimate while a description is being sketched and questionable once it is
# finished. A sequential control, 351-47-04, is the case worth allowing for: it
# runs through steps rather than holding a variable, and a model of one may
# well name none.
#
# The kind is reported alongside so the two can be told apart. OWL cannot
# require the variable under the open world assumption, so this reports rather
# than enforces.
PREFIX iec60050:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
SELECT ?control ?kind
WHERE {
  ?control a ?kind . ?kind rdfs:subClassOf* iec60050:Control .
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?control a ?narrower .
                      ?narrower rdfs:subClassOf+ ?kind ;
                                rdfs:subClassOf* iec60050:Control }
  FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?control iec60050:hasControlledVariable ?any }
} ORDER BY ?control
